{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '25745,26150p' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020025 \"C43\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020025 \"G24\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020025 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-s\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020025 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020025 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-sustained (Mmus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020025 obo:CL_0004117)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020025 obo:CL_4023032)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020025 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020026 (alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020026 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype found in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to decreases in light intensity. It is characterized by a large soma, a broad dendritic arbor that stratifies within sublamina a of the inner plexiform layer, and rapid OFF-transient firing kinetics that decay even during sustained stimulation (Krieger et al., 2017). Functionally, it corresponds to G8 in the Baden functional classification (Baden et al., 2016; Goetz et al., 2022) and C45 in the Tran transcriptomic atlas (Tran et al., 2019), and it is considered the evolutionary ortholog of the primate OFF Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). This cell type acts as a detector of rapidly approaching dark objects and contributes to innate defensive responses by encoding looming stimuli (Münch et al., 2009). It exhibits a distinctive molecular signature by its expression of Brn3c (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020026 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3493\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020026 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020026 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_0020026 \"2025-12-05T11:29:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-t\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020026 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 obo:CL_0004117)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 obo:CL_4023033)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020027 (alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-transient (Mmus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020027 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_0020027 obo:NCBITaxon_10090)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020027 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020027 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020027 \"2025-12-05T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"C41\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"G19\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-t\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020027 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020027 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-transient (Mmus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020027 obo:CL_0004117)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020027 obo:CL_4023032)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020027 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020028 (hybrid osteochondral skeletal cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30983567\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020028 \"A skeletal cell at the periosteal surface of the murine rib that displays hybrid osteochondral properties, emerging within the large callus that bridges segmental rib defects. It derives from a Sox9-expressing periosteal skeletal stem/progenitor subpopulation that constitutes only a small fraction of uninjured rib periosteum. After injury, these cells populate the callus and co-express cartilage and bone regulators Sox9 and Runx2, as well as matrix genes Col2a1 and Col1a1, while exhibiting dual chondrocyte/osteoblast properties.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_0020028 obo:NCBITaxon_10090)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020028 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020028 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020028 \"2025-12-16T14:37:04Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020028 \"hybrid osteochondral skeletal cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020028 obo:CL_0007001)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002515))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020029 (cuboidal epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020029 \"An epithelial cell that has a cuboidal morphology.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020029 <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-9765-6788>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020029 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020029 \"2025-12-16T15:56:39Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020029 \"cuboidal epithelial cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0020029 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0001872)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020029 obo:CL_0000075)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020030 (CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31207603\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31390978\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36907685\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38166256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020030 \"A CD4-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation (e.g., chronic infection, tumors, or persistent inflammation). This state is characterised by sustained expression of PD-1 as a shared feature. Additional exhaustion-associated molecules, including the transcription factor TOX, and context- or stage-dependent changes in markers such as LAG-3, TIM-3, CD39, and T-bet, may also be observed; however, the expression levels of these molecules vary depending on exhaustion stage and tissue environment.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020030 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3453>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020030 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5742-4697>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020030 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020030 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020030 \"2026-01-13T15:30:05Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020030 \"CD4+ exhausted T lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020030 \"exhausted CD4 T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020030 \"exhausted CD4-positive T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020030 \"CD4-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0020030 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000624 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001919)))\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0020030 obo:CL_0000624)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020030 obo:CL_0011025)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020031 (CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31207603\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36907685\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38166256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020031 \"A CD8-positive alpha-beta T cell that displays impaired function and altered differentiation as a result of chronic antigenic stimulation (e.g., chronic infection, tumours, or persistent inflammation). This state is characterised by sustained expression of PD-1 as a shared feature. Additional exhaustion-associated molecules, including expression of the transcription factor TOX and reduced T-bet, and context- or stage-dependent changes in markers such as LAG-3, TIM-3, CD39, and EOMES, may also be observed; however, the expression levels of these molecules vary depending on exhaustion stage and disease context.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020031 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3453>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020031 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5742-4697>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020031 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020031 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020031 \"2026-01-13T15:30:05Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020031 \"CD8+ exhausted T lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020031 \"exhausted CD8 T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020031 \"exhausted CD8-positive T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020031 \"CD8-positive exhausted alpha-beta T cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0020031 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000625 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001919)))\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0020031 obo:CL_0000625)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020031 obo:CL_0011025)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020032 (oRGC2)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020032 \"A conserved retinal ganglion cell orthotype whose transcriptomic profile groups together ON parasol RGCs from primate foveal and peripheral retina with their molecularly homologous mouse α RGC subtype (ON-transient α RGC, C41) (Hahn et al., 2023; Tran et al., 2019). Reference to the transcriptomic evidence is found at: GSE237215.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020032 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:CL_0020032 \"CL:9900000\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020032 \"oRGC2\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:label \"reference transcriptomic data on GEO\") rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0020032 \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE237215\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020032 obo:CL_0000740)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020033 (stem cell memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19525962\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28060797\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020033 \"A CD4-positive memory alpha-beta T cell with stem-like properties that is long-lived, retains a naïve-like phenotype, and exhibits self-renewal and multipotent differentiation capacity. This cell acts as a stem-like reservoir capable of regenerating central and effector memory T cell subsets.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020033 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5742-4697>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020033 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020033 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020033 \"2026-01-12T12:14:30Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"CD4+ T memory stem cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"CD4+ TSCM cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"CD4-positive TSCM cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"stem cell memory CD4+ T-cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"stem cell memory CD4+ T-lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"stem cell memory CD4+ alpha-beta T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"stem cell memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"stem cell–like memory CD4+ T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020033 \"stem cell–like memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020033 \"stem cell memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020033 obo:CL_0000897)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020034 (stem cell memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19525962\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28060797\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020034 \"A CD8-positive memory alpha-beta T cell with stem-like properties that is long-lived, retains a naïve-like phenotype, and exhibits self-renewal and multipotent differentiation capacity. This cell acts as a stem-like reservoir capable of regenerating central and effector memory T cell subsets.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020034 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5742-4697>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020034 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020034 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020034 \"2026-01-12T12:14:30Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"CD8+ T memory stem cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"CD8+ TSCM cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"CD8-positive TSCM cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"stem cell memory CD8+ T-cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"stem cell memory CD8+ T-lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"stem cell memory CD8+ alpha-beta T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"stem cell memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"stem cell–like memory CD8+ T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020034 \"stem cell–like memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020034 \"stem cell memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020034 obo:CL_0000909)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020035 (intestinal intraepithelial lymphocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29674648\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Intraepithelial_lymphocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020035 \"A T cell that is located in the intestinal epithelium and is capable of a mucosal immune response.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020035 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3455\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020035 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020035 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020035 \"2026-01-05T11:44:26Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020035 \"intestinal intraepithelial lymphocyte\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0020035 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002419 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0001025 obo:UBERON_0001277) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002385)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020035 obo:CL_0002496)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020036 (oRGC1)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020036 \"A conserved retinal ganglion cell orthotype whose transcriptomic profile groups together OFF midget RGCs from primate foveal and peripheral retina with their molecularly homologous mouse alpha RGC subtype (OFF-sustained alpha-RGC, C42) (Hahn et al., 2023; Tran et al., 2019). Reference to the transcriptomic evidence is found at: GSE237215.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020036 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020036 \"2025-12-08T11:40:49Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:CL_0020036 \"CL:9900001\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020036 \"oRGC1\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:label \"reference transcriptomic data on GEO\") rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0020036 \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE237215\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020036 obo:CL_0000740)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020037 (superficial zone articular chondrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23015907\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23124445\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41226342\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020037 \"An articular chondrocyte located in the most superficial zone of articular cartilage, characterized by flattened morphology and tangential alignment parallel to the joint surface, and residing within a matrix of fine collagen fibrils and relatively low proteoglycan content. In mice and humans, this cell typically expresses lubricin (PRG4) and contributes to lubrication and resistance to shear and tensile forces at the cartilage surface.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020037 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0098-4399>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020037 \"2026-02-18T11:06:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020037 \"superficial zone articular chondrocyte\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020037 obo:CL_1001607)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020037 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013208))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020038 (middle zone articular chondrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23015907\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23124445\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41226342\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020038 \"An articular chondrocyte located in the middle (transitional) zone of articular cartilage, characterized by round morphology and relatively random spatial organization, and residing in a matrix enriched in proteoglycans and thicker collagen fibrils oriented obliquely to the articular surface. This cell contributes to the largest volume fraction of articular cartilage and functions primarily in distributing and absorbing compressive loads between the superficial and deep zones.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020038 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0098-4399>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020038 \"2026-02-18T11:06:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23015907\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020038 \"transitional zone articular chondrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020038 \"middle zone articular chondrocyte\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020038 obo:CL_1001607)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020039 (deep zone articular chondrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23015907\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23124445\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41226342\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020039 \"An articular chondrocyte located in the deep (radial) zone of articular cartilage, characterized by columnar arrangement perpendicular to the joint surface and residence within a matrix containing the highest proteoglycan concentration and large-diameter collagen fibrils oriented radially. In humans, this cell expresses collagen type X (COL10A1) and provides maximal resistance to compressive forces. It is positioned adjacent to the tidemark, where collagen fibrils extend into the calcified cartilage to anchor the articular cartilage to subchondral bone.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020039 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0098-4399>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020039 \"2026-02-18T11:06:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23015907\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020039 \"radial zone articular chondrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020039 \"deep zone articular chondrocyte\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020039 obo:CL_1001607)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020039 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005693))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020040 (calcified zone articular chondrocyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18455690\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23015907\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:41226342\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020040 \"An articular chondrocyte located in the calcified cartilage zone below the tidemark at the interface between articular cartilage and subchondral bone, embedded within a mineralized extracellular matrix. In humans, this cell exhibits a hypertrophic-like phenotype and typically expresses collagen type X (COL10A1). Together with the surrounding calcified matrix, it forms a transitional region that mechanically couples the deep articular cartilage to the underlying subchondral bone.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020040 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0098-4399>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020040 \"2026-02-18T11:06:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020040 \"calcified zone articular chondrocyte\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020040 obo:CL_1001607)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020040 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005693))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020041 (oRGC4)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020041 \"A conserved retinal ganglion cell orthotype whose transcriptomic profile groups together ON midget RGCs from primate foveal and peripheral retina with their molecularly homologous mouse alpha RGC subtype (ON-sustained α RGC, C43) (Hahn et al., 2023; Tran et al., 2019). Reference to the transcriptomic evidence is found at: GSE237215.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020041 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:CL_0020041 \"CL:9900001\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020041 \"oRGC4\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:label \"reference transcriptomic data on GEO\") rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0020041 \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE237215\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020041 obo:CL_0000740)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020042 (oRGC5)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020042 \"A conserved retinal ganglion cell orthotype whose transcriptomic profile groups together OFF parasol RGCs from primate foveal and peripheral retina with their molecularly homologous mouse α RGC subtype (OFF-transient α RGC, C45) (Hahn et al., 2023; Tran et al., 2019). Reference to transcriptomic evidence can be found at: GSE237215.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020042 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020042 \"2025-12-08T11:46:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020042 \"oRGC5\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:label \"reference transcriptomic data on GEO\") rdfs:seeAlso obo:CL_0020042 \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE237215\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020042 obo:CL_0000740)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020043 (fasciacyte)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29575206\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33573365\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020043 \"A mesenchymal stromal cell of the deep fascia (e.g., fascia lata) that is vimentin-positive, CD68-negative, and S-100A4-positive, organized in small clusters at the interface between fibrous fascial sublayers and loose connective tissue. It is specialized for hyaluronan-rich ECM biosynthesis, as evidenced by HAS2 mRNA expression, Alcian Blue staining, and anti-HABP immunoreactivity, and functions to regulate fascial gliding and viscoelasticity.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020043 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3497>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020043 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020043 \"2026-02-20T14:27:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020043 \"Stecco et al. demonstrate that fasciacytes differ from classical fascial fibroblasts in morphology, location (small clusters at the interface between fibrous and loose fascial layers), marker profile (S-100A4 expression), and ECM output (HA-rich rather than collagen-rich).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020043 \"fasciacyte\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0020043 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000499 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0011236)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020043 obo:CL_0000499)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020044 (migratory muscle precursor)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11081511\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16977478\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21720828\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020044 \"Muscle precursor cells that delaminate from the dermomyotome after epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition (EMT) and undergo long-range migration while retaining proliferative capacity.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020044 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2244-7917>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21720828\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020044 \"MMP\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020044 \"migratory muscle precursor\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020044 obo:CL_0000680)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020044 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:UBERON_0004290))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020044 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002353 obo:GO_0001837))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020045 (Dogiel type II neuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020045 \"A neuron characterised by Dogiel type II morphology: a large, smooth, oval soma bearing multiple long axon-like processes (multiaxonal) that extend without branching until they reach their targets. The soma lacks the short lamellar or spiny dendrites characteristic of Dogiel type I neurons. Dogiel type II neurons were first described by Alexander Dogiel in 1899 based on methylene blue staining in gastrointestinal ganglia. In the enteric nervous system, Dogiel type II neurons correspond to intrinsic primary afferent neurons (IPANs) and exhibit AH-type electrophysiology (prolonged afterhyperpolarization following an action potential).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020045 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020045 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020045 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020045 \"multiaxonal enteric neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020045 \"type II enteric neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020045 \"AH neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020045 \"Dogiel II neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020045 \"Dogiel type II neuron\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020045 obo:CL_0000540)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020045 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002005))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020046 (intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37355216\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020046 \"A sensory neuron of the enteric nervous system whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus and which functions as the afferent limb of intrinsic reflex circuits controlling motility, secretion, and blood flow. This neuron is characterised by Dogiel type II morphology (large smooth soma with multiple long axon-like processes), AH-type electrophysiology (prolonged afterhyperpolarization following an action potential), and is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and immunonegative for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020046 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020046 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020046 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37355216\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020046 \"multiaxonal cholinergic myenteric sensory neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020046 \"myenteric sensory neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020046 \"IPAN\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020046 \"intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020046 obo:CL_0000101)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020046 obo:CL_0007011)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020046 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020047 (interneuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32888429\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020047 \"An interneuron of the enteric nervous system whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus. Interneurons of the myenteric plexus integrate sensory input from intrinsic primary afferent neurons (IPANs) and modulate motor output to smooth muscle and secretory epithelia by synapsing onto motor neurons and other interneurons within the plexus.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020047 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020047 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020047 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020047 \"enteric interneuron of myenteric plexus\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020047 \"interneuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020047 obo:CL_0007011)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020047 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020048 (secretomotor/vasodilator neuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32888429\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020048 \"An enteric neuron whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus and which controls mucosal secretion and blood flow by innervating secretory epithelia and submucosal blood vessels. This neuron is characterised by expression of vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP). In mouse, two Glp2r+ subtypes have been identified: PSVN1 (VIP+, non-cholinergic) and PSVN2 (ChAT+, cholinergic). In human, only the VIP+ non-cholinergic subtype has been detected.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020048 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020048 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020048 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32888429\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020048 \"VIP-positive secretomotor neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020048 \"PSVN\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020048 \"secretomotor/vasodilator neuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020048 obo:CL_0007011)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020048 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020049 (intestinofugal neuron)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38292899\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020049 \"An enteric neuron whose soma resides in the myenteric plexus of the intestine and whose axon projects outside the gut wall to synapse on neurons in prevertebral sympathetic ganglia (celiac, superior mesenteric, or inferior mesenteric ganglia). This neuron provides a pathway for gut-to-brain communication via sympathetic prevertebral ganglia. In humans, 89% are immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT); CART (cocaine- and amphetamine-regulated transcript) is NOT a human marker (0% CART+) but is present in rodent viscerofugal neurons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020049 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020049 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020049 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38292899\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020049 \"cholinergic viscerofugal neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38292899\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020049 \"viscerofugal neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38292899\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020049 \"VFN\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020049 \"intestinofugal neuron\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020049 obo:CL_0007011)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020049 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020050 (ascending interneuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020050 \"An interneuron of the myenteric plexus whose axon projects orally (in the ascending direction) along the gut axis. This neuron is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and enkephalin (ENK), and forms the excitatory limb of ascending reflex pathways that coordinate peristalsis.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020050 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020050 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020050 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020050 \"ascending myenteric interneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020050 \"cholinergic enkephalinergic myenteric interneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020050 \"ascending interneuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020050 obo:CL_0020047)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020051 (descending interneuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020051 \"An interneuron of the myenteric plexus whose axon projects aborally (in the descending direction) along the gut axis. This neuron class encompasses multiple chemically diverse subtypes including serotonergic (5-HT+), nitrergic (NOS1+), and other populations, forming the inhibitory limb of descending reflex pathways.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020051 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020051 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020051 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020051 \"descending myenteric interneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020051 \"descending interneuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020051 obo:CL_0020047)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020052 (stubby Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37355216\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020052 \"A Dogiel type I neuron of the myenteric plexus characterised by stubby (lamellar) dendrite morphology with broad, flattened dendritic expansions. This neuron is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and immunonegative for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1), corresponding to excitatory motor neurons of the enteric nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020052 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020052 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020052 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020052 \"lamellar Dogiel type I neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020052 \"stubby Dogiel I neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020052 \"stubby Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020052 obo:CL_0000100)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020052 obo:CL_0007011)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020052 obo:CL_4047038)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020052 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020053 (spiny Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37355216\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020053 \"A Dogiel type I neuron of the myenteric plexus characterised by spiny (spine-like) dendrite morphology with numerous short projections along the dendrites. This neuron is immunopositive for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1) and immunonegative for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT), corresponding to inhibitory motor neurons of the enteric nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020053 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020053 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020053 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020053 \"spiny Dogiel I neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020053 \"spiny Dogiel type I neuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020053 obo:CL_0007011)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020053 obo:CL_4047038)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020053 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002439))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020054 (Dogiel type II neuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37355216\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020054 \"An intrinsic primary afferent neuron of the myenteric plexus characterised by Dogiel type II morphology: a large, smooth, oval soma bearing multiple long axon-like processes that extend without branching until they reach their targets in both the myenteric and submucosal plexuses and the mucosa. The soma lacks the dendrites characteristic of Dogiel type I neurons and is larger in cross-sectional area than either motor neuron type. This neuron is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and immunonegative for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1). It exhibits AH-type electrophysiology, characterised by a prolonged afterhyperpolarization (AHP) following an action potential. Substance P (encoded by TAC1) expression has been reported in subsets across species.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020054 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020054 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020054 \"2026-03-10T14:42:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020054 \"AH-type myenteric neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020054 \"multiaxonal myenteric sensory neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020054 \"type II myenteric neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020054 \"Dogiel type II neuron of myenteric plexus\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020054 obo:CL_0020045)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020054 obo:CL_0020046)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020055 (calretinin-positive intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37355216\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40954253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020055 \"An intrinsic primary afferent neuron of the myenteric plexus that is immunopositive for calretinin. This neuron shares the Dogiel type II morphology and AH-type electrophysiology of all myenteric IPANs, and is immunopositive for choline acetyltransferase (ChAT) and immunonegative for neuronal nitric oxide synthase (NOS1).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020055 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3471>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020055 \"GitHub Copilot\